## Graphical Abstract
Co-Ag alloy nanoparticles were encapsulated and protected by nitrogen doped carbon (Co-Ag(n)@NC). The self-supported Co-Ag(n)@NC composites served as high-efficiency and stable catalysts exhibited excellent catalytic performances for the chemoselective hydrogenation of various functionalized nitrobenzenes using either \(\mathrm{N}_{2}\mathrm{H}_{2}\cdot\mathrm{H}_{2}\mathrm{O}\) or \(\mathrm{H}_{2}\) as green reducing agent towards synthesizing the corresponding anilines, especially the halogenated nitrobenzenes without obvious dehalogenation.
